
  <sn><md>### Tobacco and Other Addictive Substances

![img](https://researchoutreach.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/shutterstock_401380984.jpg)

* **Definition &amp; Production**: Tobacco is made by `drying the leaves` and `branches of tobacco` plants. Dried leaves are shredded and wrapped in paper to make cigarettes, biri, and churut.
* **Smoking Process**: `Inhaling the smoke and vapor` from burning tobacco products is known as **smoking**.
* **Chemical Composition &amp; Harmful Effects**:
* **Nicotine**: `Temporarily stimulates nerves` while endangering the body.
* **Toxic Gases &amp; Chemicals**: Cigarette smoke contains `narcotics and toxic gases` that `reduce the oxygen-carrying capacity of hemoglobin` in the blood.
* **Sticky Substances &amp; Hydrocarbons**: Cause various `lung diseases and cancer`.

