<sn><md>### Bad Effects of Smoking

* **Increased Disease Vulnerability**: Smokers get `sick more frequently` than non-smokers.
* **Major Health Risks**: Causes `cancers` (lung, lip, mouth, larynx, throat, urinary bladder), bronchitis, stomach ulcers, and heart/blood-related diseases. Most lung cancer patients die within five years.
	+++ ...
	![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/smoking_causes_diseases.png)
	+++
	
* **Reduced Life Expectancy**: Studies show smoking `shortens overall lifespan`.
* **Passive Smoking**: `Non-smokers` who `inhale secondhand smoke` nearby are also `adversely affected`.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Attempts to Control Smoking and Use of Tobacco Products

* **Public Place Bans**: Smoking is `illegal` in buses, trains, open fields, restaurants, offices, hospitals, and rail stations. Strict enforcement of existing anti-smoking laws is required.
* **Mandatory Warning Labels**: `Packaging must display graphic disease imagery` alongside warnings like *"Smoking is like taking poison"* or *"Smoking is harmful to health"*.
  +++ view
   ![img](https://www.shutterstock.com/image-photo/20-august-2024-bagdogra-west-260nw-2505386151.jpg)
  +++

* **Advertising Restrictions**: `Advertising` of tobacco and related products is `strictly banned`.
* **School Zone Protection**: `Sales and advertising` of cigarettes/tobacco products are `prohibited` near schools, colleges, and educational institutions.</md></sn>